# oracle: pair_style comb3 polar_off with fix qeq/comb (every step, precision 1e-4) on the same 162-atom Cu2O block as w158cb_static, initial charges from the example, 0.05 A random displacement: 10 NVE steps; per-atom forces and equilibrated charges of the final state, thermo rows
# native: installed lmp (b332f28 build, which includes COMB3). The charges are solved by fix qeq/comb each step.
# Measured error (engine vs native): worst per-atom force relative error 2.0e-12 (atom 41 fz); the equilibrated charges move by up to 0.65 from the initial ones and agree with native within the 1e-12 absolute floor (filerel 1e-15 passes).
# oracle-inputs: w158cb_cuo.data
# oracle-potentials: ffield.comb3
# oracle-files: w158cb_qeq.q
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10 atomrel=1e-8 filerel=1e-8
units		metal
atom_style	charge
dimension       3
boundary        p p p
read_data	w158cb_cuo.data
displace_atoms  all random 0.05 0.05 0.05 4417 units box
pair_style	comb3 polar_off
pair_coeff	* * ffield.comb3 Cu O
neighbor	2.0 bin
neigh_modify	every 1 delay 0 check yes
fix		1 all nve
fix		2 all qeq/comb 1 1e-4
timestep        0.00020
thermo_style	custom step temp etotal pe evdwl ecoul press vol lx ly lz
thermo_modify	norm yes format float %.15g
thermo		5
run		10
write_dump all custom w158cb_qeq.q id q modify format float %.17g sort id
